{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedStandardCount","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedStandardCount","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedAddable","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedReadback"],"declarations":24,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_uninsertSteps_of_standard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_uninsertSteps_of_standard","kind":"theorem","line":414,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L414-L432","doc":"**The recovered word rebuilds `P`, given a standard recording tableau of the same shape.**\n\nRun the reverse cascade at the positions `Q` dictates, collect what falls out, and re-inserting that\nword returns `P`.\n\nThis is word-level surjectivity on the `P` side. It is **not** bijectivity of `rskPair`: nothing\nhere says the recovered word's *recording* tableau is `Q`, and `RSKBurnsideHolds` for general `n`\nstays open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_qPositions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.addableAlong_qPositions","kind":"theorem","line":362,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L362-L400","doc":"**A standard tableau gives an addable sequence.**\n\n`hnd` supplies exactness and duplicate-free rows, `hrange` supplies totality (without which an\nabsent timestamp would read as row `0`), and `hcs` with `hstrict` supply the column comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qPositions_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qPositions_succ","kind":"theorem","line":357,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L357-L360","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.count_qPositions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.count_qPositions","kind":"theorem","line":322,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L322-L348","doc":"**The count equality.** The number of steps landing in row `i` equals the number of entries of\nrow `i` below the horizon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_qRowOf_eq_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_qRowOf_eq_iff","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L304-L320","doc":"Locating a timestamp below the horizon returns its row, as a plain `ℕ`.\n\nThe `.getD 0` in `qPositions` is why totality had to be proved: without `hrange`, an absent timestamp\nwould read as row `0` and be counted there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qPositions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qPositions","kind":"def","line":300,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L300-L302","doc":"**The position list** of the timestamps `0, …, n-1`: for each, the row of `Q` that holds it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.nodup_of_mem_of_flatten_nodup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.nodup_of_mem_of_flatten_nodup","kind":"theorem","line":290,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L290-L298","doc":"A row of a tableau with distinct entries is itself duplicate-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qRowOf_eq_some_iff_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qRowOf_eq_some_iff_mem","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L275-L278","doc":"**`qRowOf` locates exactly.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qRowOf_eq_some_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qRowOf_eq_some_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L254-L273","doc":"**Exactness.** With entries distinct across rows, membership in row `i` forces `qRowOf` to\nreturn `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qRowOf_isSome_of_mem_flatten","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qRowOf_isSome_of_mem_flatten","kind":"theorem","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L241-L252","doc":"**Totality.** A timestamp occurring anywhere in `Q` is located. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_above_qRowOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_above_qRowOf","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L222-L228","doc":"**The bridge fact, reached through `qRowOf`.** If `qRowOf` places `k` in row `r + 1`, then row\n`r` holds strictly more entries below `k` — which, read through brick 22's count shape, is exactly\nthe addability of the cell `k` occupies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qRowOf_lt_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.qRowOf_lt_length","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L206-L220","doc":"**The located row is a row.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.mem_of_qRowOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.mem_of_qRowOf","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L191-L204","doc":"**The located row contains the timestamp.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_above_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_above_mem","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L166-L177","doc":"**The bridge fact, keyed on membership.** If `k` occurs in row `r + 1`, row `r` holds strictly\nmore entries below it. This is the form the assembly reaches: it needs only the row `qRowOf`\nreturns, never a column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_countLt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.getD_countLt","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L163-L164","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_lt_length","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_lt_length","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L160-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_lt_length_and_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_lt_length_and_getD","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L142-L158","doc":"**The column of an entry is its `countLt`.** Both halves at once, since the induction is shared:\nthe count is a valid index, and reading there returns the entry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L134-L140","doc":"Nothing below the threshold means a count of zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_above","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_above","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L102-L122","doc":"**The bridge fact.** If an entry sits at column `c` of row `r + 1`, then row `r` holds strictly\nmore entries below it.\n\nColumn-strictness supplies both halves: the entry directly above is smaller, and — via the length\nhalf of `StrictBelow` — that cell exists at all. Row `r` therefore has its first `c + 1` entries\nbelow the threshold, against exactly `c` in row `r + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.lt_countLt_of_getD_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.lt_countLt_of_getD_lt","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L83-L100","doc":"An entry strictly below `k` at index `c` forces more than `c` entries below `k`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_getD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_getD","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L61-L81","doc":"**In a strictly increasing row, the entries below `row[c]` are exactly the first `c`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_cons","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_cons","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L56-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt_nil","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.countLt","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedStandardCount.lean#L51-L52","doc":"How many entries of a row lie strictly below `k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}